        "original_id": "b0ee9b94-d4bd-50ff-ab93-3e4704f5eccf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Coolio, Stevie Wonder\n- Products: Fantastic Voyage: The Greatest Hits, It Takes a Thief, Gangsta's Paradise, My Soul, Pastime Paradise, Curtain Falls\n- Topics: compilation albums, sampling\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Stevie Wonder released the song \"Pastime Paradise.\"\n- In 1995, Coolio released the hit song \"Gangsta's Paradise.\"\n- Coolio's song \"Gangsta's Paradise\" samples the chorus and instrumentation of Stevie Wonder's 1976 song \"Pastime Paradise.\"\n- The background music of \"Curtain Falls\" is almost identical to that of Coolio's \"Gangsta's Paradise\" because both songs use a sample of Stevie Wonder's \"Pastime Paradise.\"\n- In 2001, Coolio released \"Fantastic Voyage: The Greatest Hits,\" a compilation album.\n- Songs on \"Fantastic Voyage: The Greatest Hits\" originally appeared on Coolio's first three albums: \"It Takes a Thief,\" \"Gangsta's Paradise,\" and \"My Soul.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
